{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"bereaved-fertile-gull","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nBug 828a found that src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md contradicted the authoritative G6 criterion for a month without any gate noticing. The packaged prose guides cite criterion ids inline as if authoritative, but nothing couples them to the criteria registry.\n\nvalidate_criteria_guide() (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py:640-657) enforces parity only between the registry and the GENERATED docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md, scoped by _GUIDE_RELPATH. tests/unit/test_guides.py couples the guide to coach_moves.MOVE_REGISTRY only. Any criterion-text change can silently invalidate the prose guides' claims, so this drift class will recur.\n\n## Approach\nExtend the existing regenerate-in-place + parity-diff contract to cover the packaged prose guides, so a criterion change that invalidates a guide claim fails a gate rather than shipping. It reuses parity machinery already proven for the generated criteria guide, keeping one mechanism for one job.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py\n- tests/unit/test_guides.py\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A criterion-text change that contradicts a claim in a packaged prose guide fails a gate; verified by mutating a criterion in a test and asserting the gate reports the divergence.\n- [ ] The gate covers every guide in AUTHOR_GUIDES, not just the plan guide; verified by a parameterized test over AUTHOR_GUIDES.","id":"2f3c-6303-709d-49a0","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["plan-review","docs"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Gate parity between packaged prose guides and the criteria registry"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785516715943328001,"uuid":"b0b75c01-5a6e-481b-9408-0ffdcb1905cc"}